<title>INDIA: India's Oriental Bank 1996/97 net rises.</title>
<headline>India's Oriental Bank 1996/97 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     1,802    vs    1,730</p>
<p>    Shr (rupees)		 9.36 vs	  8.97</p>
<p>    Div (percent)	     25    vs	 25</p>
<p>    Net sales	     12,505    vs   11,267</p>
<p>    Other income	   1,044    vs    1,001</p>
<p>    Total expenditure    8,008    vs    9,540</p>
<p>    Operating expenses   2,534    vs    2,849</p>
<p>NOTE: A spokesman of the Oriental Bank of Commerce said that the bank had made a contingency provision of 1.2 billion rupees for 1996/97.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
